Now my bags are heavy.
I need a break.
There is a small tea shop on the side of the road.
I stop there.
I say to the tea vendor, "Bhaiya, please give me one cutting chai."
The tea seller smiles.
He says, "Yes Madam, I will give it right now."
He gives hot tea in a small glass.
I take the glass of tea.
I ask him, "Bhaiya, how much is it?"
He answers, "Ten rupees."
I open my purse.
I have loose change.
I take out ten rupees in coins.
I give him the money.
The tea is very hot and sweet.
I drink the tea slowly.
There is a lot of noise in the market.
There are many people here.
I drink tea and watch the market crowd.
